## How These Four Things Work Together

Here is the full production picture once you have all four set up:

```
Internet
   │
   ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│  Single AWS ALB              │  ← Ingress + ALB Controller
│  (one load balancer total)   │    (not one per service)
└─────────────┬───────────────┘
              │ routes by path
    ┌─────────┼──────────┐
    ▼         ▼          ▼
 api-svc   auth-svc  payment-svc
    │         │          │
    ▼         ▼          ▼
  Pods      Pods       Pods        ← deployed via Helm charts
    │                              ← IRSA gives each pod its own
    ▼                                 AWS identity, no hardcoded keys
  Nodes auto-scale               ← Karpenter adds/removes nodes
  (pay only for what you use)       based on actual pod demand
```

---

## Recommended Order to Learn These

| Order | Topic | Why this order |
|-------|-------|---------------|
| 1st | **Helm** | You'll use it to install everything else too |
| 2nd | **IRSA** | Security first — before any service touches AWS |
| 3rd | **Ingress + ALB Controller** | Save money, consolidate load balancers |
| 4th | **Karpenter** | Optimization — get cost efficiency on nodes |

